            <ArticleTitle>Posterior rounded high-intensity zone on magnetic resonance images as a sign of painful disk. Report of a case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>371-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 1992, Aprill and Bogduk reported that a rounded high-intensity zone was seen in the posterior part of the annulus fibrosus on T2-weighted images of at least one of the last intervertebral disks in 29% of 500 patients with low back pain. This image was correlated with Dallas stage 4 disk disease and with reproduction of the spontaneous pain during discography coupled with computed tomography. We report a case and discuss the value of this image.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
